It binds on high zone-1 load and is essentially extinguished by high zone-1 wind (the top-5% wind bucket kills the binding rate by 92%). Zone 4 tells the same story more weakly (load +1.83, wind −0.45), and the ordering holds at the 90% and 75% cuts too.

Tomorrow: **wind is supportive** (zone 1 off-peak 3rd pct, zone 3/4 bottom-decile through the afternoon) but **load is not** (zone 1 on-peak 33rd pct, zone 4 on-peak 6th pct). And the zone-1 evening wind ramp — 84th pct at hr21 rising to 97th at hr24 — lands squarely on the hours this thing normally binds hardest.

